### Order Service — HTTP scenarios (Step 1 dev)
### Base URL: http://localhost:8081
### Public per PDF (no auth on order-service).
### Run top-to-bottom: each request depends on variables set by the previous one.
###
### Prerequisites:
###   • order-service running on :8081
###   • restaurant-service running on :8080  (menu + proxy endpoints call it)
###   • Replace @restaurantId and @menuItemId below with REAL IDs from restaurant-service.
###     To get them: open restaurant-service's dishtest.http and run create-restaurant → create-dish → publish-dish,
###     then copy the returned UUIDs here.

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@restaurantId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@menuItemId  = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### 1. Create cart (returns cartId)
# @name createCart
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/carts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("cartId", response.body.cartId);
    client.log("cartId = " + response.body.cartId);
%}

### 2. Add item to cart (US15 / US16 — first add pins the restaurant)
# @name addItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "menuItemId":   "{{menuItemId}}",
  "itemName":     "Margherita",
  "quantity":     2,
  "unitPrice":    10.50,
  "restaurantId": "{{restaurantId}}"
}

### 3. Get cart snapshot (review before checkout, US15)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}

### 4. Update item quantity
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}/items/{{menuItemId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 3 }

### 5. List menu via proxy (US39 — symbol resolved from restaurant type)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/price-category

### 6. Checkout (US17 / US18 / US19 / US20)
# @name checkout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cartId":       "{{cartId}}",
  "customerId":   "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333",
  "customerName": "Ruben",
  "street":       "Langestraat",
  "number":       "12",
  "postalCode":   "2000",
  "city":         "Antwerpen",
  "country":      "BE",
  "email":        "ruben@example.com"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("orderId", response.body.orderId);
    client.global.set("paymentRef", response.body.paymentRef);
    client.log("orderId = " + response.body.orderId);
    client.log("paymentRef = " + response.body.paymentRef);
%}

### 7. Confirm payment (stub — calls back to webhook; US20)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentRef}}/confirm

### 8. Place order (US18 freeze; publishes order.placed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/place

### 9. Tracking (US21 — current status + history)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/tracking

### 10. Get order detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}

### 11. Cancel (only valid until ACCEPTED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "customer changed mind" }